    <!-- About -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.About_Title">About BS Group Generator</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.About_Desc">Reads the mods installed via Mod Organizer 2, lets you batch-assign BodySlide slider sets into groups, and generates group files in BodySlide's native format. Works with any BodySlide-supported game such as Skyrim SE/AE and Fallout 4.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.About_Author">Author: lin-414</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.About_Compat">The group files are fully compatible with BodySlide; each group becomes its own file named after the group, stored in BodySlide's SliderGroups folder.</sys:String>

    <!-- Help -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_H1">1. Quick start (4 steps)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_01">This tool reads the mods installed via Mod Organizer 2 (MO2), lets you batch-assign outfits (BodySlide slider sets) into groups, and generates group files in BodySlide's native format, one file per group.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_02">1. Pick the MO2 instance and Profile — global instances and portable installs are discovered automatically; the Profile defaults to the last one used.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_03">2. Confirm the BodySlide folder — auto-detection usually succeeds. The grey "effective project path" line below the cards is where BodySlide actually reads outfits and groups; keep an eye on it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_04">3. Create groups and tick — use "New group" on the right to create and select a group; tick a separator in the left tree (= all its mods) or expand and tick individual outfits; clicking "Add to group" is what actually writes. A green ✔ means the outfit is already in that group; "Remove from group" undoes ticked content.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_05">4. Save — click "Save group files" (Ctrl+S). Each group produces one file named after it (e.g. UBE.xml). Restart BodySlide afterwards (if you launch through MO2, restart MO2 too).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_H2">2. Interface areas</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_S2_Top">[Top settings area]</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_06">MO2 instance: global instances and portable installs under %LOCALAPPDATA%\ModOrganizer are found automatically; "Add MO2 folder…" points to an instance folder manually; "Refresh" rescans instances.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_07">Profile: lists every Profile available to that instance. The enabled-mod list comes from that Profile's modlist.txt, in the same order as MO2's left pane.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_08">BodySlide: searches enabled mods for folders containing BodySlide*.exe and Config.xml; if none is found, use "Browse…" to point at one.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_09">Output location: decides where group files are written (see chapter 5). The status bar shows the current output folder on the right; hover for the full path.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_S2_Tree">[Left mod tree]</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_10">Hierarchy: separator (grey) → mod (bold, collapsible) → outfits; same order as MO2's left pane, showing only enabled mods that contain BodySlide outfits.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_11">Filter boxes at the top match outfit and mod names (substring, case-insensitive); a mod-name hit shows that mod's whole outfit list; "Unassigned only" shows outfits not yet in any group.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_12">Checkboxes only "select" content — "Add to group" / "Remove from group" does the writing. Ticking a mod or separator ticks all outfits beneath it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_13">A green ✔ prefix means the outfit is already in the selected group; the [in group x/total] badge after a mod title shows how many of its outfits are in the group.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_S2_Groups">[Right group panel]</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_14">Group list: click to select (left-tree ticks and badges switch along without losing your place); double-click or "View members" opens the member preview (filterable, tick to batch-remove).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_15">"Rule grouping": batch operations by keyword — see chapter 4.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_16">"Undo" (Ctrl+Z): steps back through the last 30 grouping changes — see chapter 5.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_17">"Import group file…": merges other group XML files into the current list for editing.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_18">New-mod reminder: when a scan finds newly installed outfit mods a popup lists them by separator → mod → outfit (same as the main tree, expandable) — tick, pick a target group, click "Add selected" (undoable), and you can repeat with different target groups. Closing defers it; you can still find those outfits later via "Unassigned only".</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_S2_Status">[Status bar]</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_19">Left: counters (mods/outfits/assigned/unassigned), "Diagnostics" (instance discovery and path resolution details), "Log" (expand the run log).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_20">Right: the current output folder; hover for the full path.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_H3">3. Saving and file layout</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_21">On save, each group becomes its own file named after the group (e.g. UBE.xml), containing BodySlide's native &lt;SliderGroups&gt; format (UTF-8 with BOM), fully compatible with BodySlide.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_22">Saving again overwrites same-named group files and automatically cleans up leftovers from renamed/deleted groups via the internal manifest. Closing the app with unsaved changes shows a warning.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_23">Note: if a custom output folder is not somewhere BodySlide reads (the SliderGroups of the effective project path, or of a mod), BodySlide will not load those groups.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_H4">4. Rule grouping (batch)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_24">With large outfit counts, use keywords to round up a whole batch at once:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_25">1. Select the target group on the right; "Rule grouping" opens its own window (the main window stays usable).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_26">2. Three kinds of keywords (separate several with ;, any hit counts; case-insensitive substring match):</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_27">Mod keywords: filter candidate mods by mod name first, then search outfits within them — same-named outfits in other mods are not pulled in; empty = any mod.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_28">Outfit keywords: match by outfit name; empty = all outfits.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_29">Excluded keywords: outfits whose name matches are dropped.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_30">3. "Unassigned outfits only" leaves already-grouped ones alone; the direction is "add to" or "remove from" the group.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_31">4. The preview shows separator → mod → matched outfits (same hierarchy as the main tree) with a live "will match N outfits" count; click "Apply" to execute — Ctrl+Z undoes it. Example: mod keyword ube, exclude localisation, unassigned only → pulls all ungrouped UBE outfits into the target group in one go (outfit names need not contain ube).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_H5">5. Undo and output location</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_32">"Undo" (Ctrl+Z or the button) steps back through the last 30 grouping changes: add/remove, rule grouping, new/rename/delete group, import, and removals from the member viewer all undo. Saving does not clear undo history; restarting the app does.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_33">Five output modes:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_34">Auto (recommended): writes to the effective project path's SliderGroups when it is a real folder; when it is CalienteTools\BodySlide under MO2's virtual Data (the most common case), writes to the MO2-dedicated mod "BS Group Generator".</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_35">MO2-dedicated mod: mods\BS Group Generator\CalienteTools\BodySlide\SliderGroups\ — visible in MO2, toggleable per Profile, survives BodySlide reinstalls.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_36">BodySlide app folder / real game Data / custom: writes to the SliderGroups of the respective location.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_H6">6. FAQ</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_37">· Ticked but not in the group? Ticking only selects — click "Add to group".</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_38">· New groups not showing in BodySlide? 1) Restart BodySlide (with MO2, restart MO2 too); 2) open Settings → Diagnostics and compare the "effective project path" with your "output folder" — BodySlide only reads groups from the effective project path's SliderGroups.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_39">· Why are some mods missing? The tree only shows enabled mods containing BodySlide outfits; disabled mods or mods without outfits do not appear.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_40">· (name conflict) after an outfit name? That outfit name appears in several mods; ownership is displayed for the highest-priority mod, but grouping matches by name and is unaffected.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_41">· What is BSGroupGenerator.files.txt in the output folder? The tool's manifest, used to clean up old files automatically; BodySlide ignores it.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L.Help_42">· Something crashed? Exceptions are written to %APPDATA%\BSGroupGenerator\crash.log — feel free to send that file to the developer.</sys:String>
